<body>
<div class="poster">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="venue">Nature Research Conference · Neuroscience Symposium</div>
    <div class="citation">Published in Nature, 2024 &nbsp;|&nbsp; DOI: 10.1038/s41586-024-07487-w</div>
    <h1>Mapping Neural Circuit Architecture:<br>Advances in Brain Connectivity Analysis</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive connectomics study revealing new principles of neural circuit organization through large-scale structural and functional mapping</div>
  </div>

  <!-- METRICS BANNER -->
  <div class="metrics-banner">
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-icon">🧠</div>
      <div class="metric-value">~125,000</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Neurons Mapped</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Total neurons reconstructed in the connectome dataset</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-icon">🔗</div>
      <div class="metric-value">~54 Million</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Synaptic Connections</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Individual synapses identified and catalogued</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-icon">🧩</div>
      <div class="metric-value">37</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Circuit Motifs</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Distinct recurring connectivity motifs discovered</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card">
      <div class="metric-icon">🎯</div>
      <div class="metric-value">94.2%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Classification Accuracy</div>
      <div class="metric-context">Automated neuron-type classification performance</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- BACKGROUND -->
  <div class="background-section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="num">01</span>
      Background &amp; Motivation
    </div>
    <div class="background-grid">
      <div class="background-text">
        <p>Understanding how the brain processes information requires detailed maps of neural connectivity. While classical neuroanatomy provided foundational insights, the field has long lacked the resolution and scale needed to capture complete circuit-level wiring diagrams.</p>
        <p>Recent advances in electron microscopy, automated segmentation, and computational neuroscience have converged to make large-scale connectomics feasible. This study bridges the gap between structural connectivity and functional organization at unprecedented scale.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="background-highlight-box">
        <h3>Why This Study Matters</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>First connectomic map at this scale and resolution</li>
          <li>Multi-modal pipeline combining imaging, ML, and functional validation</li>
          <li>Open-access dataset released to accelerate community discovery</li>
          <li>Bridges structural wiring to functional circuit principles</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- METHODS PIPELINE -->
  <div class="methods-section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="num">02</span>
      Methodology &amp; Technical Approach
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">🔬</div>
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <h4>Imaging</h4>
        <p>Serial-section electron microscopy at 4 × 4 × 30 nm resolution</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">🤖</div>
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <h4>Segmentation</h4>
        <p>Deep learning-based automated neuron tracing with human proofreading</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">🧠</div>
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <h4>Synapse Detection</h4>
        <p>Convolutional neural network classifier (94.2% accuracy)</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">📊</div>
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <h4>Circuit Analysis</h4>
        <p>Graph-theoretic motif detection and clustering algorithms</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-icon">⚡</div>
        <div class="step-num">5</div>
        <h4>Validation</h4>
        <p>Calcium imaging and optogenetic perturbation experiments</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- KEY FINDINGS -->
  <div class="findings-section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="num">03</span>
      Key Findings
    </div>
    <div class="findings-grid">
      <div class="finding-card">
        <div class="finding-highlight">Circuit Architecture</div>
        <div class="finding-metric">37 Motifs</div>
        <h3>Modular Wiring Logic</h3>
        <p>37 distinct connectivity motifs were identified as recurring building blocks of larger circuits, suggesting the brain employs a finite vocabulary of circuit elements — analogous to logic gates in digital circuits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="finding-card">
        <div class="finding-highlight">Network Topology</div>
        <div class="finding-metric">3.5% → 28%</div>
        <h3>Hub Neuron Dominance</h3>
        <p>Hub neurons comprising only ~3.5% of the population accounted for over 28% of total synaptic output, indicating a highly non-uniform distribution of influence across the network.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="finding-card">
        <div class="finding-highlight">Layer-Specific Rules</div>
        <div class="finding-metric">4.7:1</div>
        <h3>Recurrent-to-Feedforward Ratio</h3>
        <p>Feedforward connections dominated between layers 2/3→4, while recurrent connections were enriched within layer 5 (4.7:1 recurrent-to-feedforward ratio).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="finding-card">
        <div class="finding-highlight">Cell-Type Wiring</div>
        <div class="finding-metric">6.2×</div>
        <h3>Inhibitory Specificity</h3>
        <p>Inhibitory interneurons formed connections with 6.2× higher specificity than excitatory neurons, challenging previous assumptions of broad inhibitory blanket coverage.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- IMPLICATIONS -->
  <div class="implications-section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <span class="num">04</span>
      Implications &amp; Future Directions
    </div>
    <div class="implications-grid">
